  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "$\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u=1-{x}^{3}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{x}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,(-\\frac{2}{3})\\text{d}u=2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{3}}}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(2\\sqrt{u})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
